# Testing

Vitest with `globals: true` (no need to import `describe`/`it`/`expect`) and the
`jsdom` environment. `src/test/setup.ts` stubs browser APIs missing from jsdom
(`ResizeObserver`, `matchMedia`, `Element.scrollTo`).

## Conventions

- Co-locate tests in a `tests/` folder next to the code, named `*.test.ts(x)`.
- Test through the public interface and assert on user-visible behavior, not
  implementation details.

## Component tests

- Use `@testing-library/react` (`render`, `screen`) and `@testing-library/user-event`.
- Query by accessible role and name (`screen.getByRole('switch', { name: 'Toggle' })`),
  not by test ids or class names.
- `cleanup()` runs automatically after each test.

## Mocking the Electron bridge

- Components that read `window.electronApi` must install the fake bridge with
  `installMockElectronApi(options)` from `@test/electronApi`; drive IPC callbacks
  with the returned `emitStream` / `emitFullScreenChange` helpers.
- Tear down with `clearMockElectronApi()` when a test mutates the global.

## Main-process tests

- Pure logic (`main/model`, `main/logger`, `main/locale`) is unit-tested directly;
  keep such logic free of Electron singletons so it stays testable.
